link2symlink: take a link off its group once the rename or unlink succeeded

The count of a faked hard link went down at the entry of rename(2) and
unlink(2), whatever came of the syscall. "mv new existing" calls
renameat2(RENAME_NOREPLACE) first, which fails as the destination exists,
then rename(): two links were taken off for the one that was replaced, and
with two links in the group the file behind them was deleted, leaving the
other link dangling. A program that saves a file by renaming a temporary
one over it (a package upgrade in a uv or pnpm environment, whose files are
links into the cache) lost the other copies that way. Any rename or unlink
that failed (EXDEV, EACCES, ENOTDIR) miscounted too.

The entry stage now only remembers the group of the link about to go, and
the exit stage counts it down if the syscall returned 0. renameat2 with
RENAME_NOREPLACE or RENAME_EXCHANGE never removes its destination and
remembers nothing.

